      "writtenOn": "2024-09-06T18:46:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To Jason:\n\nThat was the intention. I will document it in the code.\n\nTo Serdar:\n\nI was thinking about if we could do \"lazy initialization\" but later I am confused with the word \"externally synchronized\". Is it allowed to \"vkWaitForFences\" on thread A first and later submit and signal the fence on thread B?\n\nI could not confirm the answer, so I decided to do it in the safe way. But let me know if you know for sure this is not allowed, then we can do the lazy init.",
      "parentUuid": "d25fa4f2_85b51f68",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 293,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 294,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "8653c1e8a2e1b9819281f3cb71caf59607b02586",
